== 3. eigenvalues are minus Kloosterman sums: max |lambda_a + Kl(N(a))| over q ==
q = 7: max deviation 8.88e-16
q = 11: max deviation 1.78e-15
q = 13: max deviation 3.11e-15
q = 29: max deviation 7.11e-15
q = 31: max deviation 7.99e-15
q = 101: max deviation 1.60e-14
Weil |Kl(n)| <= 2 sqrt(q) then gives |lambda| <= 2 sqrt(q) for every nontrivial character.
smallest prime with 1 + (q+1)/(2 sqrt q) > 6: 101 (value 6.0747); at 97: 5.9752
exact threshold: (q+1)/(2 sqrt q) > 5 iff sqrt q > 5 + sqrt 24 = 9.898979 iff q > 97.9898
at q = 239: 1 + 240/(2 sqrt 239) = 8.7622 ; at q = 149^3: 910.4
